      "library": "org.springframework:spring-aop:6.1.7",
      "summary": "Failure is a genuine upstream behavior change, not a setup gap: Spring removed AbstractAspectJAdvisorFactory.compiledByAjc()/its ajc$-marker check between 6.1.0 and 6.1.7, so isAspect() now accepts AJC-compiled-marker classes it used to reject. The 6.1.0 test still asserts the old rejection behavior. No new Maven dependency, Docker image, or env/system property is needed — the resolved dependency graph (POM) is identical aside from version bumps, and the operation involved (AnnotationUtils.findAnnotation) is plain reflection with no Native Image implications.",
      "deterministic_setup": [],
      "agent_guidance": "The failing assertion in AbstractAspectJAdvisorFactoryTest.rejectsAnnotationStyleAspectWithAjcCompiledMarkerField encodes 6.1.0-era behavior (isAspect() used to call a private compiledByAjc(Class<?>) helper that scanned declared fields for an 'ajc$' prefix and rejected such classes). That helper and the check were removed in AbstractAspectJAdvisorFactory by 6.1.7 (org/springframework/aop/aspectj/annotation/AbstractAspectJAdvisorFactory.java), so isAspect() now returns true for AjcCompiledMarkerAspect. This is a test logic update, not an environment/dependency/Docker setup gap.",
